  "summary": "Preprints pair Rydberg phase estimation and finite-interaction CCZ gates with fault-tolerant T-gate and many-body control schemes.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is extending what neutral-atom Rydberg hardware can do beyond ideal operation. One preprint demonstrates quantum phase estimation on an analog Rydberg simulator, extracting ground-state energies and gaps for up to 19 atoms via the Loschmidt echo. Another proposes an analytically specified CCZ gate under finite Rydberg interactions, outside the strong-blockade regime, and compares it with a fast antiblockade scheme. Related items address broader control and architecture: a persistent-mediator color-code design for repeated logical T gates, Krotov optimal control of GHZ-type states with one local field in an XXZ chain, a Fe2+:forsterite qubit proposal, and Majorana-based reservoir computing. These latter works are not Rydberg-specific; they share an emphasis on protected or controllable quantum resources, and all are preprint-stage proposals or simulations apart from the demonstrated phase estimation.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-19"
